# Application

One use-case per file: `{verb}.use-case.ts`, `{Verb}UseCase.execute`. Tests: [tdd](./tdd.mdc).

A use-case is either an **endpoint** (same `{verb}` on contract, router, and [container](./container.mdc)) or the **implementation of a port method** (called from the provider adapter, not exposed on the contract).

## Logic

- Policy & workflow (uniqueness, order of steps)
- `AppError` + `ERROR_CODES`
- Service for calculations and tech (hash, windows, formatting). Use-case orchestrates and applies policy
- A state change is recorded through `AuditLogService` in the same transaction. See [shared](./shared.mdc)
- Input/output = shared dto types, not local aliases

Repo reports facts; use-case turns them into policy.

## Do

- Inject collaborator types (`AuthService`, `UserPort`, your repository)
- Cross-module via port only. The port returns **their** DTO; you load **your** rows and `Mapper.toDto`
- No foreign ids → `[]` and skip your query

## Shape

Return the aggregate or the list. Do not add an endpoint whose only job is one field.

```ts
// find-organization-name.use-case.ts
execute(): Promise<{ name: string }>;

// find-organizations.use-case.ts
execute(): Promise<OrganizationDto[]>;
```

The client reads `organization.name` off `findOrganizations`.

## Shared logic

Do not add `application/*.util.ts` for policy shared by several use-cases in the same module. Prefer a small [service](./service.mdc) wired in [container](./container.mdc) and injected; or private methods on each use-case (duplication OK); or [entity](./entity.mdc) pure methods when there is no `AppError` / I/O. One-off helpers in `application/` are discouraged.

## Shared logic

Do not add `application/*.util.ts` for policy shared by several use-cases in the same module. Prefer a small [service](./service.mdc) wired in [container](./container.mdc) and injected; or private methods on each use-case (duplication OK); or [entity](./entity.mdc) pure methods when there is no `AppError` / I/O. One-off helpers in `application/` are discouraged.

## Don't

- Drizzle / tables / oRPC / other module's repo
- Ask another module to query or return your aggregate
- `create({ email, password })` on a repo that has an entity — that is `Factory` + `save` in the **provider** use-case (or service), not in the [port impl](./port-adapter.mdc)

```ts
async execute(input: CreateUserInputDtoType): Promise<CreateUserOutputDtoType> {
  const existing = await this.userPort.findByEmail(input.email);
  if (existing) throw new ConflictError(ERROR_CODES.EMAIL_ALREADY_TAKEN);

  const passwordHash = await this.authService.hashPassword(input.password);
  return await this.userPort.create({ email: input.email, name: input.name, passwordHash });
}
```

```ts
async execute(input: FindOrdersInputDtoType): Promise<FindOrdersOutputDtoType> {
  const users = await this.userPort.findManyByOrganizationId({ organizationId: input.organizationId });
  if (users.length === 0) return [];

  const orders = await this.orderRepository.findManyByUserIds(users.map((user) => user.id));
  return orders.map((order) => OrderMapper.toDto(order));
}
```
